/-!
# Places with separable residue field

Let `F / k` be an algebraic function field over an **infinite** field `k`, separable over a
rational subfield `k(x)`.  Then `F` has a place `P` whose residue field is a separable extension of
`k` of degree at most `[F : k(x)]`.  Geometrically, a smooth curve over an infinite field has a
closed point with separable residue field, of degree bounded by the degree of any separable map to
the projective line.

The place is found over a rational place of `k(x)`, of which there are infinitely many since `k` is
infinite, at which the minimal polynomial of a primitive element of `F / k(x)` has separable
reduction, which holds away from finitely many places.  Kummer's theorem at such a place
(`TauCeti.Place.exists_restrict_eq_relativeDegree_eq_and_isSeparable`) produces places of `F`
above it whose residue fields are generated by a root of a separable irreducible factor of the
reduction.

**In genus zero the degree bound is two.**  If `F / k` has genus zero, exact constant field and a
separating element, then `F` is separable over some `k(x)` of index at most two.  Indeed, an
anticanonical divisor `B` can be taken effective, of degree two, with `ℓ(B) ≥ 3`, and every
nonconstant function in `L(B)` has index at most two.  Away from characteristic two such an index
is separable.  In characteristic two, if two functions `x, z ∈ L(B)` with `1, x, z` independent
both had inseparable index two, then every square of `F` would lie in `k(x) ∩ k(z)`, so the
separating element would force `k(x) = k(z)`.  But a function of `k(x)` whose poles are bounded by
`(x)_∞` is a polynomial of degree at most one in `x`.  So every genus-zero function field with
exact constant field and a separating element over an infinite field has a place of degree at most
two with separable residue field.  Geometrically, a smooth proper curve of genus zero over an
infinite field has a closed point whose residue field is separable of degree at most two over `k`.
Over that residue field the curve has a rational point, and a curve of genus zero with a rational
point is the projective line
(`TauCeti.nonempty_algEquiv_ratFunc_of_genus_eq_zero_of_divisor_degree_eq_one`); this is the input
for nodal reduction of curves of genus zero over a discrete valuation ring.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.exists_place_degree_le_finrank_and_isSeparable`: a function field over an infinite
  field, separable over `k(x)`, has a place of degree at most `[F : k(x)]` with residue field
  separable over `k`.
* `TauCeti.exists_degree_eq_two_and_three_le_dim_of_genus_eq_zero`: a genus-zero function field
  with exact constant field has an effective divisor `B` of degree two with `ℓ(B) ≥ 3`.
* `TauCeti.exists_finrank_adjoin_le_two_and_isSeparable_of_genus_eq_zero`: a genus-zero function
  field with exact constant field and a separating element is separable over a rational subfield
  of index at most two.
* `TauCeti.exists_place_degree_le_two_and_isSeparable_of_genus_eq_zero`: **a genus-zero function
  field with exact constant field and a separating element over an infinite field has a place of
  degree at most two whose residue field is separable over `k`**.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Chapter 55, Semistable Reduction](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C2P),
  the case of genus zero.
* H. Stichtenoth, *Algebraic Function Fields and Codes*, 2nd ed., GTM 254, Springer, 2009,
  Theorem 3.3.7 (Kummer's theorem).
-/

public section

open Polynomial

open scoped IntermediateField

namespace TauCeti

open AlgebraicGeometry

variable {k F : Type*} [Field k] [Field F] [Algebra k F]

/-! ### Separable places over a separable rational subfield -/

/-- **A function field over an infinite field, separable over a rational subfield `k(x)`, has a
place of degree at most `[F : k(x)]` whose residue field is separable over `k`.** -/
theorem exists_place_degree_le_finrank_and_isSeparable [Infinite k] (hF : IsFunctionField k F)
    (x : F) [Algebra.IsSeparable k⟮x⟯ F] :
    ∃ P : Place k F, P.degree ≤ Module.finrank k⟮x⟯ F ∧ Algebra.IsSeparable k P.ResidueField := by
  classical
  have : Algebra.Transcendental k F := Algebra.transcendental_def.mpr hF.exists_transcendental
  have hx : Transcendental k x := transcendental_of_isAlgebraic_adjoin
  have : FiniteDimensional k⟮x⟯ F := hF.finiteDimensional_adjoin hx
  have hF₁ : IsFunctionField k k⟮x⟯ := hx.isFunctionField_adjoin
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Field.exists_primitive_element k⟮x⟯ F
  -- A rational place of `k(x)` at which the minimal polynomial of `y` has separable reduction.
  obtain ⟨P₁, hP₁, hgood⟩ := ((Place.infinite_setOf_degree_eq_one_adjoin hx).sdiff
    (Place.finite_setOf_not_exists_map_eq_and_separable hF₁ (minpoly k⟮x⟯ y)
      (Algebra.IsSeparable.isSeparable k⟮x⟯ y))).nonempty
  obtain ⟨φ, hmin, hsep⟩ := not_not.mp hgood
  have hφ : φ.Monic := Polynomial.monic_of_injective (IsFractionRing.injective P₁.integers k⟮x⟯)
    (hmin ▸ minpoly.monic (IsIntegral.of_finite k⟮x⟯ y))
  set res := IsLocalRing.residue P₁.integers
  have hφ0 : φ.map res ≠ 0 := (hφ.map res).ne_zero
  have hdeg : (φ.map res).natDegree = Module.finrank k⟮x⟯ F := by
    rw [hφ.natDegree_map, ← natDegree_map_eq_of_injective
      (IsFractionRing.injective P₁.integers k⟮x⟯), hmin,
      ← IntermediateField.adjoin.finrank (IsIntegral.of_finite k⟮x⟯ y), hy,
      IntermediateField.finrank_top']
  -- A monic irreducible factor `γ` of the reduction, and Kummer's theorem at `P₁`.
  have hunit : ¬IsUnit (φ.map res) := fun h ↦ by
    have := natDegree_eq_zero_of_isUnit h
    rw [hdeg] at this
    exact Module.finrank_pos.ne' this
  obtain ⟨γ, hγ⟩ := UniqueFactorizationMonoid.exists_mem_normalizedFactors hφ0 hunit
  obtain ⟨hirr, hmonic, hdvd⟩ := (Polynomial.mem_normalizedFactors_iff hφ0).mp hγ
  obtain ⟨P, hP, hrel, hsepres⟩ := Place.exists_restrict_eq_relativeDegree_eq_and_isSeparable
    (k' := k) hF₁ P₁ hy hmin hsep hmonic hirr hdvd
  subst hP
  refine ⟨P, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Place.degree_eq_degree_restrict_mul_relativeDegree k k⟮x⟯ P, hP₁, one_mul, hrel, ← hdeg]
    exact natDegree_le_of_dvd hdvd hφ0
  · -- The residue field of the rational place below is `k`, so separability goes up the tower.
    have : Algebra.IsSeparable k (P.restrict k k⟮x⟯).ResidueField :=
      AlgEquiv.Algebra.isSeparable (Place.residueFieldEquivOfDegreeEqOne _ hP₁)
    exact Algebra.IsSeparable.trans k (P.restrict k k⟮x⟯).ResidueField P.ResidueField

/-! ### Genus zero -/

/-- **A function of `k(x)` whose poles are bounded by those of `x` lies in `k + k x`**: inside the
rational function field `k(x)`, the Riemann–Roch space of `(x)_∞` contains `1` and `x` and has
dimension at most `deg (x)_∞ + 1 = 2`, and membership descends from `F` to `k(x)`. -/
private theorem mem_span_pair_of_mem_adjoin (hF : IsFunctionField k F) {x : F}
    (hx : Transcendental k x) {z : F} (hzx : z ∈ k⟮x⟯)
    (hz : z ∈ riemannRochSpace (Divisor.poles hF (Units.mk0 x fun h ↦ hx (h ▸ isAlgebraic_zero)))) :
    z ∈ Submodule.span k {1, x} := by
  set x₀ := IntermediateField.AdjoinSimple.gen k x
  have hK₀ : IsFunctionField k k⟮x⟯ := hx.isFunctionField_adjoin
  have hex₀ : IsIntegrallyClosedIn k k⟮x⟯ := hx.isIntegrallyClosedIn_adjoin
  have : FiniteDimensional k⟮x⟯ F := hF.finiteDimensional_adjoin hx
  have hx₀ : Transcendental k (x₀ : k⟮x⟯) :=
    (transcendental_algebraMap_iff (algebraMap k⟮x⟯ F).injective).mp hx
  set u : k⟮x⟯ˣ := Units.mk0 x₀ fun h ↦ hx₀ (h ▸ isAlgebraic_zero)
  -- In `k(x)`, the pole divisor of `x` has degree `[k(x) : k(x)] = 1`, so `ℓ((x)_∞) ≤ 2`.
  have hdeg : Divisor.degree (Divisor.poles hK₀ u) = 1 := by
    rw [Divisor.degree_poles hK₀ u hx₀, Units.val_mk0,
      IntermediateField.adjoin_adjoinSimple_gen_eq_top, IntermediateField.finrank_top,
      Nat.cast_one]
  have hdim : Divisor.dim (Divisor.poles hK₀ u) ≤ 2 := by
    have := Divisor.dim_le_degree_posPart_add_one hK₀ hex₀ (Divisor.poles hK₀ u)
    rw [posPart_eq_self.mpr (Divisor.isEffective_poles hK₀ u).zero_le, hdeg] at this
    omega
  -- So `L((x)_∞) = k + k x` inside `k(x)`.
  have hind : LinearIndependent k ![(1 : k⟮x⟯), x₀] := by
    refine LinearIndependent.pair_iff.mpr fun s t hst ↦ ?_
    by_cases ht : t = 0
    · subst ht
      simpa using hst
    · refine absurd ⟨C t * X + C s, fun h0 ↦ ht ?_, ?_⟩ hx₀
      · simpa using congrArg (coeff · 1) h0
      · simpa [Algebra.smul_def, add_comm] using hst
  have hspan : Submodule.span k {(1 : k⟮x⟯), x₀} = riemannRochSpace (Divisor.poles hK₀ u) := by
    have hcard := finrank_span_eq_card hind
    rw [Matrix.range_cons_cons_empty, Fintype.card_fin] at hcard
    have := finiteDimensional_riemannRochSpace hK₀ (Divisor.poles hK₀ u)
    refine Submodule.eq_of_le_of_finrank_le ?_ (by rw [hcard, ← Divisor.dim_def]; exact hdim)
    rw [Submodule.span_le, Set.insert_subset_iff, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact ⟨one_mem_riemannRochSpace_iff.mpr (Divisor.isEffective_poles hK₀ u).zero_le,
      mem_riemannRochSpace_poles hK₀ u⟩
  -- The function `z` descends to `L((x)_∞)` computed in `k(x)`.
  have hw : (⟨z, hzx⟩ : k⟮x⟯) ∈ riemannRochSpace (Divisor.poles hK₀ u) := by
    have hu : Units.map (algebraMap k⟮x⟯ F : k⟮x⟯ →* F) u =
        Units.mk0 x fun h ↦ hx (h ▸ isAlgebraic_zero) := Units.ext rfl
    have h := mem_riemannRochSpace_nsmul_poles_map_iff (k' := k) hK₀ hF 1 u ⟨z, hzx⟩
    rw [one_nsmul, one_nsmul, hu] at h
    -- `algebraMap k⟮x⟯ F ⟨z, hzx⟩` is `z` by definition.
    exact h.mp hz
  rw [← hspan, Submodule.mem_span_pair] at hw
  obtain ⟨a, b, hab⟩ := hw
  rw [Submodule.mem_span_pair]
  exact ⟨a, b, by simpa [x₀] using congrArg (algebraMap k⟮x⟯ F) hab⟩

/-- **A function field of genus zero with exact constant field has an effective divisor of degree
two whose Riemann–Roch space has dimension at least three.**  Such a divisor lies in the
anticanonical class, and `ℓ(B) = deg B + 1 - g = 3`. -/
theorem exists_degree_eq_two_and_three_le_dim_of_genus_eq_zero (hF : IsFunctionField k F)
    (hex : IsIntegrallyClosedIn k F) (hg : genus k F = 0) :
    ∃ B : Divisor k F, 0 ≤ B ∧ Divisor.degree B = 2 ∧ 3 ≤ Divisor.dim B := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW⟩ := exists_isRiemannRochDivisor hF hex
  have hdegW : Divisor.degree W = -2 := by simpa [hg] using hW.degree_eq hF hex
  have hdimW : (3 : ℤ) ≤ Divisor.dim (-W) := by
    have := Divisor.degree_add_one_sub_genus_le_dim hF (-W)
    rw [Divisor.degree_neg, hdegW, hg] at this
    simpa using this
  obtain ⟨B, hB, hequiv⟩ := (riemannRochSpace_ne_bot_iff hF (D := -W)).mp (by
    rw [ne_eq, ← Divisor.dim_eq_zero_iff_riemannRochSpace_eq_bot hF]
    omega)
  refine ⟨B, hB, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← Divisor.degree_eq_of_linearlyEquivalent hF hequiv, Divisor.degree_neg, hdegW]
    rfl
  · rw [← Divisor.dim_eq_of_linearlyEquivalent hF hequiv]
    omega

/-- **A genus-zero function field with exact constant field and a separating element is separable
over a rational subfield of index at most two.** -/
theorem exists_finrank_adjoin_le_two_and_isSeparable_of_genus_eq_zero (hF : IsFunctionField k F)
    (hex : IsIntegrallyClosedIn k F) (hg : genus k F = 0) (t : F) [Algebra.IsSeparable k⟮t⟯ F] :
    ∃ x : F, Module.finrank k⟮x⟯ F ≤ 2 ∧ Algebra.IsSeparable k⟮x⟯ F := by
  -- Take an effective `B` of degree two with `ℓ(B) ≥ 3`: any nonconstant `x ∈ L(B)` has
  -- `[F : k(x)] = deg (x)_∞ ≤ 2`.  Away from characteristic two `F / k(x)` is then separable; in
  -- characteristic two one of `x` and `z` works, for `x, z ∈ L(B)` with `1, x, z` independent.
  obtain ⟨B, hB, hBdeg, hdimB⟩ := exists_degree_eq_two_and_three_le_dim_of_genus_eq_zero hF hex hg
  have hBeff : WeilDivisor.IsEffective B := WeilDivisor.isEffective_iff_zero_le.mpr hB
  -- A nonconstant `u ∈ L(B)` is transcendental, with `(u)_∞ ≤ B`, so `[F : k(u)] ≤ 2`.
  have hindex (u : F) (huB : u ∈ riemannRochSpace B) (hu : u ∉ k ∙ (1 : F)) :
      ∃ hu0 : u ≠ 0, Transcendental k u ∧ Divisor.poles hF (Units.mk0 u hu0) ≤ B ∧
        Module.finrank k⟮u⟯ F ≤ 2 := by
    have hut : Transcendental k u := fun halg ↦ by
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := isIntegrallyClosedIn_iff_forall_isAlgebraic.mp hex u halg
      exact hu (hc ▸ Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mpr ⟨c, by simp [Algebra.smul_def]⟩)
    have hu0 : u ≠ 0 := fun h ↦ hut (h ▸ isAlgebraic_zero)
    have hle := (poles_le_iff_mem_riemannRochSpace hF hBeff (Units.mk0 u hu0)).mpr huB
    refine ⟨hu0, hut, hle, ?_⟩
    have := Divisor.degree_le_of_le hle
    rw [Divisor.degree_poles hF (Units.mk0 u hu0) hut, hBdeg] at this
    exact_mod_cast this
  -- Two functions `x, z ∈ L(B)` with `1, x, z` linearly independent.
  have := finiteDimensional_riemannRochSpace hF B
  rw [Divisor.dim_def] at hdimB
  obtain ⟨x, hxB, hx1⟩ : ∃ x ∈ riemannRochSpace B, x ∉ k ∙ (1 : F) := by
    by_contra! h
    have := Submodule.finrank_mono (show riemannRochSpace B ≤ k ∙ (1 : F) from h)
    rw [finrank_span_singleton one_ne_zero] at this
    omega
  obtain ⟨z, hzB, hzx⟩ : ∃ z ∈ riemannRochSpace B, z ∉ Submodule.span k {(1 : F), x} := by
    by_contra! h
    have : FiniteDimensional k (Submodule.span k {(1 : F), x}) :=
      FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite k (Set.toFinite _)
    have := Submodule.finrank_mono (show riemannRochSpace B ≤ Submodule.span k {1, x} from h)
    have hpair := finrank_range_le_card (R := k) ![(1 : F), x]
    rw [Matrix.range_cons_cons_empty, Fintype.card_fin, Set.finrank] at hpair
    omega
  obtain ⟨hx0, hxt, hxle, hx2⟩ := hindex x hxB hx1
  obtain ⟨-, hzt, -, hz2⟩ := hindex z hzB fun h ↦ hzx (Submodule.span_mono
    (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr (Set.mem_insert _ _)) h)
  by_cases hxs : Algebra.IsSeparable k⟮x⟯ F
  · exact ⟨x, hx2, hxs⟩
  by_cases hzs : Algebra.IsSeparable k⟮z⟯ F
  · exact ⟨z, hz2, hzs⟩
  -- Otherwise both indices are two and `k(x) = k(z)`, so `z ∈ k(x)`.
  exfalso
  have := hF.finiteDimensional_adjoin hxt
  have := hF.finiteDimensional_adjoin hzt
  have hx2' := Algebra.finrank_eq_two_of_not_isSeparable hx2 hxs
  have hxz := IntermediateField.eq_of_finrank_eq_two_of_not_isSeparable t hx2' hxs
    (Algebra.finrank_eq_two_of_not_isSeparable hz2 hzs) hzs
  have hzmem : z ∈ k⟮x⟯ := hxz ▸ IntermediateField.mem_adjoin_simple_self k z
  -- But `(x)_∞ = B`, both having degree two, so `z ∈ L((x)_∞)` would lie in `k + k x`.
  have hpoles : Divisor.poles hF (Units.mk0 x hx0) = B := by
    by_contra hne
    have hpos := Divisor.degree_pos hF (sub_nonneg.mpr hxle) (sub_ne_zero.mpr (Ne.symm hne))
    rw [Divisor.degree_sub, hBdeg, Divisor.degree_poles hF (Units.mk0 x hx0) hxt, Units.val_mk0,
      hx2'] at hpos
    simp at hpos
  exact hzx (mem_span_pair_of_mem_adjoin hF hxt hzmem (hpoles ▸ hzB))

/-- **A genus-zero function field with exact constant field and a separating element, over an
infinite field, has a place of degree at most two whose residue field is separable over `k`.**
Geometrically, a smooth proper curve of genus zero over an infinite field has a closed point whose
residue field is a separable extension of degree at most two. -/
theorem exists_place_degree_le_two_and_isSeparable_of_genus_eq_zero [Infinite k]
    (hF : IsFunctionField k F) (hex : IsIntegrallyClosedIn k F) (hg : genus k F = 0) (t : F)
    [Algebra.IsSeparable k⟮t⟯ F] :
    ∃ P : Place k F, P.degree ≤ 2 ∧ Algebra.IsSeparable k P.ResidueField := by
  obtain ⟨x, hx2, hxs⟩ := exists_finrank_adjoin_le_two_and_isSeparable_of_genus_eq_zero hF hex hg t
  obtain ⟨P, hP, hsep⟩ := exists_place_degree_le_finrank_and_isSeparable hF x
  exact ⟨P, hP.trans hx2, hsep⟩

end TauCeti
